			"Message": "docs(Air): refresh README with problem-first messaging\n\nReplace the technical implementation focus with developer benefit messaging. Add a problem statement (VS Code cold-starts, restart prompts) followed by the solution value proposition (\"No restart prompt ever\").\n\nKey changes:\n- Open with problem-solution framing in a blockquote\n- Consolidate features into four concise bullet points covering pre-staged updates, pre-indexed workspaces, warm caches, and no restart prompt\n- Remove verbose sections: Deep Dive, System Architecture, Ecosystem table, Getting Started with usage patterns\n- Add See Also section linking to architecture overview, Why Rust, Mountain, and Echo\n- Switch Rust icon source from simpleicons.org to editor.land hosted SVG for consistency\n\nImproves developer onboarding by leading with the \"why\" before the \"how\".",
